{
  "requirement": "The source tools identify project files with project-relative `PathBuf` values.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet file = std::path::PathBuf::from(\"src/auth.rs\");\n```\n\nAn item within that file uses the path and selector in `OutlineData` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The only structural obligation in `requirements.sdk.sources.source_addresses` is the clause \"The source tools identify project files with project-relative `PathBuf` values\". A String-based path would break it, because a file would then no longer be a `PathBuf`. Item addresses are delegated to `requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity` through a {cite}, so they add no obligation here.\n\nThe supplied roots carry the obligation:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs#struct[TextMatch]` declares `pub path: PathBuf`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs#struct[StructuralMatch]` declares `pub node: crate::outline::OutlineData`, which holds the `path` and `selector` that the cited address requirement defines.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs#impl[Sources]/fn[list]` returns `Vec<PathBuf>`. It builds each one with `PathBuf::from(id.location)`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs#impl[Sources]/fn[read]` and `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs#impl[Sources]/fn[parse]` take `impl AsRef<Path>`, which accepts a `PathBuf`. They convert it with `project_resource`, so the project-relative id handling stays out of the file identity.\n\nThe remaining source tools need no marker of their own:\n- `Sources::search_text` and `Sources::search_structure` only delegate. They return `TextMatches` and `StructuralMatches`, which are `SearchResults` of the marked match types, so the match types' fields fix the `PathBuf` identity.\n- The `PathBuf::from(&id.location)` conversions in `search_text_with` and `search_structure_with` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs` are forced by those struct fields. Producing a value the marked types require does not need its own reference.\n- `SourceScope` holds a prefix `String` that selects files. It does not identify one, so the clause does not cover it.\n\nI found no structural obligation missing implementation evidence.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has two observable obligations. First, the source tools identify project files with project-relative `PathBuf` values. Second, an item within a file is identified by the `OutlineData` path and selector. The second obligation is governed by `requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity`, which is cited only, so I did not reassess that requirement.\n\n**Project-relative `PathBuf` identification**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[scoped_inspection_skips_unrelated_directories_and_reports_relevant_ignore_errors]` asserts that `list` returns `Path::new(\"src/one.txt\")`. That is a nested path relative to the root.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository]` checks listed paths such as `src/nested.txt` and `keep.txt` through `to_str()`. It also checks that `search_text` match paths are relative, with `scoped.matches[0].path == Path::new(\"src/nested.txt\")`. It uses `file(name)` and `PathBuf` inputs for `read` and `parse`, and it rejects `..` scopes.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` covers `read` of a relative path, `read` of `../outside.txt`, and `read` of an absolute path. The last two must fail, so only project-relative paths identify files. It also asserts that `parse(&file(\"note.txt\")).id().path` equals `Path::new(\"note.txt\")`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[local_provider_scopes_paths_and_rejects_resources_outside_its_root]` is also marked for this requirement. It covers listing, reading and scoping, and it rejects absolute, `..` and symlink escapes.\n\n**Item addressing by path and selector in `OutlineData`**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` asserts `parsed.id().path` and `parsed.id().selector == \"\"` for a whole file.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope]` asserts that structural matches carry `node.path == visible.rs` and `node.selector == \"fn[visible]\"`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/search.rs#fn[outline_addresses_validate_selectors_without_reading_paths]` asserts that `OutlineData::new` preserves the path and selector and rejects invalid selectors.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[addresses_preserve_opaque_fields_and_compare_each_identity_component]` checks identity components.\n\nThe tests exercise the required behavior and assert its outcomes. I found no unacknowledged gap.",
