        "rationale": "The requirement has two observable obligations. First, the source tools identify project files with project-relative `PathBuf` values. Second, an item within a file is identified by the `OutlineData` path and selector. The second obligation is governed by `requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity`, which is cited only, so I did not reassess that requirement.\n\n**Project-relative `PathBuf` identification**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[scoped_inspection_skips_unrelated_directories_and_reports_relevant_ignore_errors]` asserts that `list` returns `Path::new(\"src/one.txt\")`. That is a nested path relative to the root.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository]` checks listed paths such as `src/nested.txt` and `keep.txt` through `to_str()`. It also checks that `search_text` match paths are relative, with `scoped.matches[0].path == Path::new(\"src/nested.txt\")`. It uses `file(name)` and `PathBuf` inputs for `read` and `parse`, and it rejects `..` scopes.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` covers `read` of a relative path, `read` of `../outside.txt`, and `read` of an absolute path. The last two must fail, so only project-relative paths identify files. It also asserts that `parse(&file(\"note.txt\")).id().path` equals `Path::new(\"note.txt\")`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[local_provider_scopes_paths_and_rejects_resources_outside_its_root]` is also marked for this requirement. It covers listing, reading and scoping, and it rejects absolute, `..` and symlink escapes.\n\n**Item addressing by path and selector in `OutlineData`**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` asserts `parsed.id().path` and `parsed.id().selector == \"\"` for a whole file.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope]` asserts that structural matches carry `node.path == visible.rs` and `node.selector == \"fn[visible]\"`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/search.rs#fn[outline_addresses_validate_selectors_without_reading_paths]` asserts that `OutlineData::new` preserves the path and selector and rejects invalid selectors.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[addresses_preserve_opaque_fields_and_compare_each_identity_component]` checks identity components.\n\nThe tests exercise the required behavior and assert its outcomes. I found no unacknowledged gap."
